# Day 44

**40km / 10 hours**

Up early for a decent day ahead which began on the road before transferring to a shared cycle/quad/walking track. This was nice since it was a comfortable track to walk on without any traffic. It also had some nice scenery with the pleasant trees and plants around. 

![Isn't this a nice vibe?](./road-plants.avif)

This continued for a few hours before coming to an intersection where there was a detour for a section that had been washed out by a slip a few years prior. However the main track was walkable so we took that route instead of the slightly suspect detour. The track around the slip was quite muddy and difficult to traverse but doable. After about 22km there was a small stream crossing and the trail went off the main road which meant that it became steeper, muddier and generally harder to continue on.

![The river before crossing although there was a nicer spot to cross than this one](./river.avif)

After a decent climb then a sharp descent there was a proper river crossing after which we had a proper lunch. The river crossing was fairly comfortable with the water not too deep or fast to feel dangerous. After that section there was just more ascending in preparation for the mountain tomorrow, although it was pretty slow. For the final 7km or so it was an agonising road walk with light showers at times. It was painful primarily because of how monotonous it felt but tomorrow should be the opposite of that.

![The mountain in the clouds for tomorrow which could be very rainy](./road-mountain.avif)
